{
  "abstract": "We construct a one-parameter family of explicit algebraic correspondences between K3 surfaces that change the rational Witt index of their transcendental intersection forms. Put $D(s)=s^5-5s^3+5s$ and let $X_\\pm(c)$ be the smooth minimal models of $y^2=(s\\pm2)(x^3-3x+c(D(s)-2)+2)$, with $c\\ne0,1$. A common dihedral cover gives an actual correspondence $F:T(X_+)_{\\mathbf Q}\\to T(X_-)_{\\mathbf Q}$ with $F^\\dagger F=3+r$, where $r^2+r-1=0$, and an explicit algebraic inverse. Fiber components and pullback sections determine rank-six visible complements $H\\oplus\\langle1,-2,-5,-10\\rangle$ and $H^2\\oplus\\langle-2,-10\\rangle$. The latter embeds in Floccari's quadratic-space criterion. His theorem and the inverse correspondence prove the rational Hodge conjecture on all powers of both surfaces and their fixed-parameter mixed products. We also prove that the positive real-multiplication twist preserves the Kuga–Satake isogeny class; the known Hodge conjecture on the abelian side then gives algebraicity of the Kuga–Satake correspondence for both signs. At $c=3$, independent finite-field counters and distinct Artin–Tate squareclasses at 7 and 11 prove Picard rank 16 and exact non-CM endomorphism field $\\mathbf Q(\\sqrt5)$. The plus surface therefore supplies a concrete non-CM example with Witt index one. The result does not settle the general Hodge conjecture.",
